- Staleness (engine/migrations/053_staleness.sql, engine/src/Core/MemoryStaleness.cs): 14 days for a volatile memory
  and 90 for a state one before it may be out of date, a bounded nightly pass that finds those, one stale queue that
  its count and its list both read, and still true, which confirms a memory without changing it, after Second Brain's
  volatility, staleness pass, stale queue and still_true (src/memory/volatility.ts, src/staleness/pass.ts,
  src/memory/stale.ts, src/memory/actions.ts); volatility only as the caller gave it (no heuristic), the pass's place
  per scope on the nightly runner, a mark that holds only at the revision it was made at, and still true keeping every
  version are Rhythm's own.
- Link upkeep (engine/migrations/056_link_upkeep.sql, engine/src/Core/MemoryLinkPruning.cs): an automatic link under a
  weight of 0.3 pruned once it has gone 7 days unchecked, a link someone stated never deleted by a job and reported when
  its end is gone, after Second Brain's graph pass and graph statistics (src/graph/pass.ts, src/routes/admin.ts); a
  change of a memory's words invalidating the links drawn from them, the pass's place per scope on the nightly runner,
  a link with an end in the trash left for the restore, and the broken links counted rather than listed are Rhythm's
  own.
- Links on save (engine/migrations/062_links_on_save.sql, engine/src/Core/MemoryLinkInference.cs): a saved memory linked
  to at most 3 of its workspace's closest memories, relates_to, or follows when both are episodic and the earlier was
  written within 30 minutes and is the only one so, the score as the link's weight, and the same again when its words
  change, after Second Brain's edge inference on write (src/graph/edges.ts); the threshold re-derived per model from
  labelled pairs, the link kept automatic until a person makes it, a pair someone dismissed never linked again, held,
  trashed and replaced memories left out, and an out-of-date automatic link drawn again rather than duplicated are
  Rhythm's own.
- As-of recall (engine/src/Core/RecallAsOf.cs, engine/src/Core/Recall.cs): what was true at a past moment with every
  correction made since, a memory's words of then from the states it keeps, a belief of then marked wrong since listed
  under the true answers and never among them, at most three, newest retraction first, found through a supersede link
  too, after Second Brain's as-of recall (src/recall/as-of.ts); leaving out a memory held then, from before it came into
  the reader's scope or whose state then is no longer kept, and a catalog record answering only when unchanged since,
  are Rhythm's own.
- Digests (engine/migrations/054_digests.sql, engine/src/Core/MemoryDigests.cs): a digest of one project or one topic
  tag in one scope, drawn from its long tail of memories by upstream's rule (importance under 4, recalled never, or
  fewer than twice and over 60 days old, not a digest, not in a capsule slot, not held), at least 10 and
  the 50 newest of them, one a day, and the digest tool that reads the newest, after Second Brain's compression and
  digest tool (src/compression/eligibility.ts, src/compression/digest.ts, src/mcp/server.ts); the paragraph written by
  the AI client from the engine's list and saved with that list's basis, every source left untouched and linked by
  drawn_from instead of marked rolled up, a memory flagged by a retracted source left out, and a save from the same
  basis answering the digest saved from it are Rhythm's own.
- Open loops (engine/migrations/058_loops.sql, engine/src/Core/MemoryLoops.cs): a memory tagged task and not
  task:done is an open loop unless an agent's build-log tag marks it, a commitment is owed to or by the person with the
  other person's name kept as a slug of it, and a loop is resolved done, received or not a task, after Second Brain's
  open-loops queue, two-way commitments and resolve actions (src/memory/loops.ts, src/commitments/direction.ts,
  src/capture/t7-capture.ts, src/memory/actions.ts); the direction and counterparty kept by the engine beside the
  memory rather than in its tags, one predicate that every count and list reads, a resolve kept as a version that undo
  takes back, a Family admin never listed another member's commitments, and a name that reads like instructions
  refused are Rhythm's own.
- The decision ledger (engine/migrations/060_decisions.sql, engine/src/Core/MemoryDecisions.cs): a decision saved with
  a confidence rounded to 0.05 within 0.05 to 0.95, stated or inferred, and a review date 90 days on; an outcome right,
  wrong, mixed or unknown, unknown asking again twice; and calibration that folds a call below 50% onto the other
  outcome, counts mixed as half, bands the folded confidences, reads a Brier score and an 80% Wilson interval, names at
  most one topic, and shows nothing below minimums of 10, 5 and 5 decisions, after Second Brain's decision capture,
  outcome action and calibration (src/decisions/capture.ts, outcome.ts, queries.ts, calibration.ts,
  src/memory/actions.ts); the confidence and outcome kept by the engine beside the memory rather than in reserved tags,
  an outcome recorded as a change of state that undo takes back with no note written into the memory, one predicate
  for every list and count with calibration's sample count equal to its scored list's length, a held decision never
  scored, the band figures withheld below their minimum rather than returned unshown, and every review date a calendar
